 "parsed": {
  "count": 1,
  "rationale": "Zero controls is not enough. With no defences, the attacker can phish to get foothold_workstation and stolen_user, then pivot_internal, auth_appserver (mfa_user never blocks this, since foothold_workstation is always true), kerberoast_dc (stolen_admin), auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db and exfiltrate_db. One control is enough: mfa:admin. Data exfiltration requires admin_db or admin_fileserver, and both need stolen_dbadmin (or admin_dc, which itself requires foothold_dc). stolen_dbadmin only comes from dump_dbadmin_dc, which needs admin_dc, which needs foothold_dc. auth_dc is the only way to get foothold_dc, and it needs NOT mfa_admin. Deploying mfa:admin therefore cuts every path to exfiltration."
 },
